# GPU fan curve for dallas, fitted 2026-11-15 from Strata load/idle tests at 150 W cap.
# Points are "GPU temp C:fan %", linear in between, flat outside. Hottest GPU wins.
# Idle (Strata loaded, ~33 W/GPU): 20% held ~43 C; 10% climbed past 55 C.
# Load (~100-150 W/GPU): 60% held ~46-48 C; 40% reached 55 C and still rising.
# v2 (same day): v1 40:10,44:20,46:35,48:60,50:100 with 30 s hold and 2%/2 s drop hunted 5.4k-9.9k rpm under load.
# v2 CURVE=40:10,43:20,45:40,47:60,49:80,51:100 held <50 C but was too loud at max.
# v3: cards up to ~75 C are fine; quiet first. 82 C+ = 100% on the raw reading.
CURVE=50:10,60:15,66:20,70:30,73:40,76:60,79:80,82:100
INTERVAL=2
TAU_S=10
HOLD_S=60
DOWN_STEP=0.5
CHANNELS=1
